{
  "title": "Piano Practice",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Read",
      "lines": [
        "Notes scroll right",
        "to left on a treble",
        "staff. Play the pad",
        "as the note crosses",
        "the line.",
        "",
        "On time: the",
        "notehead turns into",
        "a circle. Missed: it",
        "turns into an X.",
        "",
        "A circle also marks",
        "where you actually",
        "played. In time, it",
        "lands on the note as",
        "one mark. Late, you",
        "see two and the gap",
        "is your error.",
        "",
        "Miss a note and the",
        "scroll stops and",
        "names it on screen.",
        "Guided, the pad you",
        "need pulses white.",
        "",
        "Miss a note and the",
        "scroll stops on it.",
        "The X stays by the",
        "line however far",
        "ahead you are",
        "reading."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Home",
      "lines": [
        "Home is where the",
        "module opens: five",
        "circles, Learning",
        "Path, Practice,",
        "Quiz, Progress and",
        "Settings. The chosen",
        "one is filled and",
        "grown, its name",
        "under it.",
        "",
        "JOG   choose",
        "CLICK open",
        "PAD   open: its",
        "      lit pad, on",
        "      the bottom row",
        "MENU  help",
        "BACK  leave",
        "",
        "The pads make no",
        "sound at home. Back",
        "from a section finds",
        "its circle chosen.",
        "",
        "SHIFT+CLICK, then",
        "Show as list: the",
        "five as a list, for",
        "the session. BACK",
        "goes back to the",
        "circles.",
        "",
        "Practice and Quiz",
        "are rings too.",
        "Practice: Scales",
        "(stairs), Chords,",
        "Progressions, Random",
        "(a die) and Songs (a",
        "note). Quiz: Ear,",
        "Reading (a staff)",
        "and Keys (a key with",
        "its letter), on the",
        "middle three pads.",
        "The same keys work;",
        "BACK goes home, on",
        "the circle you left.",
        "Deeper folders are",
        "lists."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Lessons",
      "lines": [
        "Behind each circle",
        "of home the list is",
        "in folders. CLICK",
        "opens one, BACK goes",
        "up one; BACK at home",
        "leaves. The line at",
        "the bottom always",
        "says which keys",
        "work.",
        "",
        "Learning Path",
        "  five stages, a few",
        "  weeks each, then",
        "  Review. Continue",
        "  is PLAY on its",
        "  map, and the first",
        "  row of its list.",
        "Practice",
        "  Scales, Chords,",
        "  Progressions,",
        "  Random, and Songs:",
        "  Classics,",
        "  Electronic,",
        "  Techno, Styles.",
        "Quiz",
        "  Ear: name a sound.",
        "  Reading: off the",
        "  staff. Keys: names",
        "  and pads.",
        "Progress",
        "  how far you have",
        "  got.",
        "Settings",
        "  Octave, Click,",
        "  Key, Scale and",
        "  Start at, on one",
        "  page; Advanced:",
        "  Practice, Sound,",
        "  MIDI, Help.",
        "",
        "Every row shows how",
        "far you have got: a",
        "percent, a half",
        "circle for Guided, a",
        "tick for Solo.",
        "",
        "Every song fits one",
        "page of pads, both",
        "hands."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Help",
      "lines": [
        "MENU is help, on",
        "every screen: a row",
        "of the list, the",
        "armed piece, a quiz,",
        "a result, the",
        "settings. It says",
        "what is in front of",
        "you, what its words",
        "mean, and its keys.",
        "",
        "JOG scrolls. BACK or",
        "MENU closes it, back",
        "to where you were.",
        "",
        "A quiz's clock stops",
        "while you read, and",
        "a running piece",
        "pauses.",
        "",
        "The first time you",
        "open a kind of",
        "practice, its help",
        "shows by itself.",
        "Settings > Advanced",
        "> Help > Auto info",
        "turns that off.",
        "",
        "Quiz sounds: a chime",
        "when right, an uh-oh",
        "when wrong."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Options",
      "lines": [
        "SHIFT+CLICK on a row",
        "of the list opens",
        "its options. Only",
        "what fits the row is",
        "offered:",
        "",
        "I know this: skip",
        "  a step, or",
        "  Continue's.",
        "I know it all: skip",
        "  everything in a",
        "  stage, unit or",
        "  exercise.",
        "Undo skip",
        "  takes a skip back.",
        "Start the path here",
        "  Continue starts at",
        "  this stage; the",
        "  ones before count",
        "  as known.",
        "Test out: checkpoint",
        "  plays the stage's",
        "  exam Solo. Pass it",
        "  and the path moves",
        "  on.",
        "Show as list",
        "  home, or a map, as",
        "  a list. Show as",
        "  map goes back.",
        "Settings...",
        "  the settings.",
        "",
        "JOG choose, CLICK do",
        "it, BACK close.",
        "",
        "After Guided, a skip",
        "moves on instead:",
        "Guided is enough for",
        "now."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Levels",
      "lines": [
        "A song has up to",
        "four levels, and is",
        "one row: it opens on",
        "its ready screen,",
        "first level not yet",
        "learned. The JOG",
        "walks the levels and",
        "Guided or Solo:",
        "1G 1S 2G 2S...",
        "The LEVEL box shows",
        "it: a big digit, G",
        "or S, and a tick",
        "once it is learned.",
        "",
        "L1 RH melody",
        "  the right hand",
        "  alone, one note at",
        "  a time.",
        "L1 LH bass",
        "  the left hand",
        "  alone, the bass",
        "  line.",
        "L2 RH chords",
        "  the melody with",
        "  its chords under",
        "  it.",
        "L3 Both hands",
        "  the two together.",
        "",
        "All four sit in the",
        "same register. The",
        "pads you learn at L1",
        "are the pads you",
        "play at L3.",
        "",
        "A new level starts",
        "again from bar 1. A",
        "Learning Path step",
        "and a review arm",
        "their own level.",
        "",
        "A chord lesson's L1",
        "RH is its top voice,",
        "L1 LH the roots.",
        "Inversions are one",
        "hand, so they have",
        "two."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Guided, Solo",
      "lines": [
        "Every exercise is",
        "played twice.",
        "",
        "Guided",
        "  the pad you need",
        "  next lights up as",
        "  the note comes.",
        "  Learn the shape.",
        "Solo",
        "  nothing lights up.",
        "  Read it from the",
        "  staff.",
        "",
        "90% or better",
        "passes, at any",
        "tempo. Guided earns",
        "a half circle, Solo",
        "a tick.",
        "",
        "An exercise opens on",
        "the first one you",
        "have not passed.",
        "Turn the JOG on the",
        "ready screen to pick",
        "the other - you can",
        "go straight to Solo.",
        "On a song the JOG",
        "walks the levels",
        "too.",
        "",
        "Score: notes hit",
        "over notes plus",
        "wrong presses. A row",
        "shows your latest",
        "run, but once passed",
        "it never drops.",
        "",
        "Only a run from the",
        "top counts. Start",
        "from a scrubbed bar",
        "to practise a",
        "passage off the",
        "record.",
        "",
        "In a quiz, Guided is",
        "a round with hints,",
        "Solo a round",
        "without."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Learning Path",
      "lines": [
        "The Learning Path is",
        "five stages, for",
        "adults new to the",
        "piano and the Move.",
        "Nothing is locked:",
        "play anything, in",
        "any order. It",
        "counts.",
        "",
        "1 Grid and staff",
        "2 Four chords",
        "3 Shapes and time",
        "4 Sevenths",
        "5 Colour",
        "",
        "A stage is units,",
        "each one strand:",
        "grid, read, chords,",
        "ear, pieces, hands",
        "or scales. They run",
        "find, hear, learn,",
        "use, show: the piece",
        "comes last. Then the",
        "stage's Checkpoint,",
        "its exam.",
        "",
        "Continue - PLAY on",
        "the map, or the",
        "first row of its",
        "list - opens the",
        "next step of the",
        "ready unit whose",
        "strand you played",
        "longest ago, in your",
        "stage. When a review",
        "is due, one review,",
        "then one new step.",
        "",
        "Review brings back",
        "finished exercises:",
        "any that slipped",
        "under 90%, then ones",
        "due again - after 1,",
        "3, 7, 14, then 30",
        "days. A repeat never",
        "lowers a finished",
        "score."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Map",
      "lines": [
        "The Learning Path",
        "and each of its",
        "stages are maps. On",
        "the world, an island",
        "per stage; on an",
        "island, a place per",
        "unit, and a fort for",
        "its checkpoint.",
        "",
        "A lit pad is a",
        "place. Press it to",
        "walk there, again to",
        "go in. Dark pads are",
        "water. On a map the",
        "pads make no sound.",
        "",
        "JOG   walk",
        "CLICK go in",
        "BACK  up a level",
        "PLAY  Continue",
        "MENU  help, and the",
        "      place's why",
        "",
        "The title says where",
        "you stand, how far",
        "you have got there,",
        "and the reviews due.",
        "",
        "A filled hill is",
        "done ground; a flag,",
        "done. A dotted",
        "outline was skipped.",
        "",
        "SHIFT+CLICK, then",
        "Show as list: the",
        "same folder as a",
        "list, Review in it.",
        "Show as map goes",
        "back.",
        "",
        "The way moves with",
        "you. CLICK into an",
        "island zooms in;",
        "BACK zooms out to",
        "the world.",
        "",
        "Finish a place and",
        "Next shows its flag,",
        "then your walk to",
        "the next place.",
        "Finish a stage, or",
        "pass its checkpoint:",
        "fireworks, out to",
        "the world, the sail",
        "to the next island",
        "and in. A level",
        "learned for the",
        "first time gets a",
        "star round its",
        "score.",
        "",
        "Any key or pad skips",
        "a scene, straight to",
        "where it was going."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Quiz",
      "lines": [
        "The Quiz folder has",
        "three, by skill:",
        "Ear, Reading, Keys.",
        "",
        "Keys > four drills",
        "Notes by alphabet",
        "and Chords by name",
        "show the name only:",
        "any octave or",
        "inversion counts.",
        "Name notes and Name",
        "chords light a pad:",
        "name it.",
        "",
        "Reading > courses",
        "then Notes by staff",
        "and Chords by staff:",
        "play the written",
        "notes. Each is a",
        "row: play the first",
        "and it moves on, the",
        "next ones in view.",
        "No tempo: it waits",
        "for you. A round is",
        "timed.",
        "",
        "Ear > by topic",
        "Pitch & melody,",
        "Intervals, Chords,",
        "Scales & keys. The",
        "courses sit in their",
        "topic: Identify and",
        "Compare intervals,",
        "Identify scales.",
        "Each is a numbered",
        "list of units that",
        "adds a little at a",
        "time.",
        "",
        "Reading > the",
        "courses",
        "The Ear courses",
        "again, on the staff:",
        "name the interval,",
        "compare two, name",
        "the scale. Count",
        "letters for the",
        "size, then the",
        "accidentals. PLAY",
        "sounds it, and",
        "counts as help.",
        "",
        "Ear > Play it back",
        "The same, but you",
        "hear it instead of",
        "seeing it. The staff",
        "shows a ? until you",
        "play it right, then",
        "it reveals what it",
        "was.",
        "",
        "Both drill finding a",
        "pitch on the grid,",
        "which is its own",
        "skill: the pads go",
        "up in fifths, so the",
        "same note sits in",
        "several places.",
        "",
        "A chord must be held",
        "all at once. Part of",
        "it down is not yet a",
        "mistake.",
        "",
        "Keys > Name notes,",
        "Name chords",
        "A pad lights and you",
        "name it, choosing",
        "with the jog. Click",
        "to answer. The other",
        "two are near misses",
        "- a semitone away,",
        "or the same chord",
        "root with another",
        "quality - so a rough",
        "sense of high or low",
        "will not do.",
        "",
        "This is the only",
        "mode that goes pad",
        "to name, and the",
        "only one you can do",
        "without playing.",
        "",
        "PLAY   hear it",
        "REC    help, twice",
        "BACK",
        "  back to the list",
        "",
        "Half tones adds the",
        "black notes to the",
        "note pools. On by",
        "default: they are",
        "the hard ones to",
        "find.",
        "",
        "Chords: triads asks",
        "the diatonic triads",
        "of the key. types",
        "asks a chosen",
        "quality - dim, aug,",
        "sus, 6, 7, maj7, m7,",
        "m7b5, dim7, add9.",
        "advanced adds ninths",
        "and altered",
        "dominants: 9, maj9,",
        "m9, 6/9, 7b5, 7#5,",
        "7b9, 7#9, 7sus4,",
        "9sus4, mMaj7.",
        "",
        "Both the chord",
        "symbol and its notes",
        "are shown, so you",
        "learn what the shape",
        "under your hands is",
        "called. A scale that",
        "stacks something",
        "that is not a chord",
        "shows the notes with",
        "no symbol.",
        "",
        "The answer is never",
        "lit on the pads.",
        "Guided lights pads",
        "for playing, never",
        "in a quiz.",
        "",
        "REC gives help, two",
        "presses deep.",
        "Hearing: names it,",
        "then lights the",
        "pads. Reading:",
        "sounds it, then",
        "lights the pads.",
        "Picking: strikes out",
        "one wrong option,",
        "then the other.",
        "",
        "Hinted answers still",
        "count and keep the",
        "streak, but the",
        "round records how",
        "many you took."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Answers",
      "lines": [
        "An Ear drill that",
        "asks what you heard",
        "turns the bottom",
        "pads into answer",
        "buttons, each its",
        "own colour. The",
        "screen says which is",
        "which.",
        "",
        "2-4 answers: every",
        "other pad, so a near",
        "miss hits a dark",
        "pad. 5-8: the whole",
        "bottom row. 9-12:",
        "two rows. The screen",
        "then draws a map of",
        "the pads.",
        "",
        "Press a pad to",
        "answer. It plays no",
        "note. The other pads",
        "still play.",
        "",
        "JOG and CLICK work",
        "too. The jog's",
        "answer pulses on its",
        "pad.",
        "",
        "Name keeps the jog:",
        "its lit pads are the",
        "question and stay",
        "pressable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Hearing",
      "lines": [
        "Quiz > Ear, and the",
        "Ear units of the",
        "Learning Path. You",
        "hear something and",
        "name it - nothing to",
        "read, nothing lit.",
        "Easiest first:",
        "",
        "1 Higher or lower",
        "2 Play it back",
        "3 Step or leap",
        "4 Melody shape",
        "5 Major/minor chord",
        "6 Four triads",
        "7 Major or minor key",
        "8 Home or away",
        "9 Scale degrees",
        "10 Seventh chords",
        "11 Chords in a key",
        "12 Play the chord",
        "",
        "Intervals and scales",
        "are courses: Ear >",
        "Intervals and Ear >",
        "Scales & keys, and",
        "the Ear units.",
        "",
        "Each has levels,",
        "easy to hard:",
        "melodic before",
        "together, up before",
        "down, broken chords",
        "before block ones.",
        "",
        "Press its answer",
        "pad. The answers",
        "keep their order, so",
        "where one sits",
        "becomes habit. A",
        "long list scrolls;",
        "the marks at the",
        "right say there is",
        "more.",
        "",
        "The root changes",
        "every time: listen",
        "to the distance, not",
        "the note.",
        "",
        "Right: the pads",
        "flash and the notes",
        "are named. Wrong:",
        "counted once, and",
        "the question stays.",
        "",
        "PLAY   hear it again",
        "REC    help, twice",
        "BACK",
        "  back to the list",
        "",
        "REC 1 plays it",
        "slower, chords",
        "broken up first. REC",
        "2 strikes out a",
        "wrong answer.",
        "",
        "Play it back and",
        "Play the chord are",
        "played back on the",
        "pads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rounds",
      "lines": [
        "A quiz is a round of",
        "20 prompts (10/20/30",
        "in settings, or",
        "endless).",
        "",
        "The clock starts on",
        "your first press,",
        "not when the screen",
        "appears. A prompt",
        "waits until you get",
        "it right, so a wrong",
        "answer costs you",
        "time rather than a",
        "penalty - the same",
        "way a typing test",
        "treats a typo.",
        "",
        "The result is",
        "correct answers per",
        "minute and % right.",
        "Turn the jog: RIGHT",
        "% plots success over",
        "every round; then",
        "ANSWERS shows each",
        "one - a bar over all",
        "rounds, a tick for",
        "this round, and its",
        "right/asked.",
        "",
        "endless records",
        "nothing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Results",
      "lines": [
        "A finished run shows",
        "the percent you got",
        "right and a chart of",
        "every recent",
        "attempt: hollow",
        "points are Guided,",
        "solid ones Solo. The",
        "dotted line is 90%.",
        "",
        "REC  play it again",
        "BACK",
        "  back to the start,",
        "  then BACK to the",
        "  list",
        "CLICK",
        "  next: Solo if you",
        "  just passed",
        "  Guided, else the",
        "  next step",
        "SHIFT+CLICK",
        "  move on, or skip",
        "  it",
        "",
        "Progress: Overall",
        "and each stage plot",
        "steps passed over",
        "time. Then",
        "everything you",
        "played, newest",
        "first. CLICK a row",
        "for its chart, JOG",
        "for the next.",
        "",
        "A quiz drill plots",
        "its rate as a line",
        "and its errors as",
        "bars. A full bar is",
        "50% wrong."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Play",
      "lines": [
        "PLAY",
        "  listen. The",
        "  exercise plays",
        "  itself and the",
        "  pads light up as",
        "  it goes, so you",
        "  can watch it",
        "  before you try it.",
        "  Nothing scored.",
        "REC",
        "  practice. You play",
        "  it, it scores you.",
        "",
        "Both pulse when",
        "ready. The one that",
        "is running goes",
        "solid.",
        "",
        "KNOB 1 scrubs",
        "through the piece",
        "before you start,",
        "and the pads light",
        "the note you landed",
        "on. PLAY or REC then",
        "begins from where",
        "you left it, with no",
        "count-in and no",
        "misses for the bars",
        "you skipped over.",
        "BACK returns to the",
        "top.",
        "",
        "JOG",
        "  pick, in the list",
        "CLICK",
        "  open the folder",
        "MENU   help",
        "BACK   up one level",
        "SHIFT + BACK   close",
        "",
        "SHIFT+CLICK:",
        "settings",
        "",
        "Four beats count you",
        "in, counted on",
        "screen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sound",
      "lines": [
        "The module has its",
        "own piano. It is the",
        "default and needs no",
        "setup: no track, no",
        "instrument, no MIDI",
        "channel to match. It",
        "mixes in alongside",
        "whatever else Move",
        "is playing.",
        "",
        "MIDI out can send",
        "elsewhere instead:",
        "track",
        "  a Move track, on",
        "  the MIDI ch below",
        "  (all = every",
        "  channel)",
        "USB",
        "  the USB-A port",
        "trk+USB",
        "  both of those",
        "",
        "Closing silences the",
        "piano and every",
        "channel on both MIDI",
        "routes, then waits",
        "for it to drain",
        "before letting go.",
        "SHIFT + BACK closes",
        "from anywhere."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Settings",
      "lines": [
        "Settings is the last",
        "circle of home: one",
        "short page of what",
        "is yours. Octave",
        "(where the pads",
        "start), Click, Key",
        "and Scale (what the",
        "free library is made",
        "in) and Start at",
        "(where the Learning",
        "Path starts). CLICK",
        "a row to edit it,",
        "turn to change,",
        "CLICK again when",
        "done.",
        "",
        "Advanced, the last",
        "row, holds the rest",
        "in groups: Practice,",
        "Sound, MIDI and",
        "Help. BACK goes back",
        "a step at a time.",
        "",
        "SHIFT+CLICK on a",
        "piece opens this",
        "page; SHIFT+CLICK",
        "again, on any",
        "settings page, goes",
        "straight back to the",
        "piece.",
        "",
        "Wait stops the",
        "scroll at a note",
        "until you play it.",
        "On by default.",
        "",
        "The scroll always",
        "halts ON the note it",
        "wants, so you can",
        "see what it is",
        "asking for. A missed",
        "chord is named under",
        "the staff, not over",
        "it.",
        "",
        "PLAY again pauses",
        "where you are. Knob",
        "1 scrubs whenever",
        "the music is not",
        "running - paused, or",
        "before you begin -",
        "smoothly, about 1.5",
        "turns per bar. PLAY",
        "carries on from",
        "there, so you can",
        "take a bar twice.",
        "BACK restarts; twice",
        "leaves. Knob 8 is",
        "tempo.",
        "",
        "Grace is how late",
        "you may play it and",
        "still count, in",
        "beats - so it scales",
        "with tempo. One beat",
        "by default: time to",
